# The real keyboard and mouse through Horizon (no KEYS script, the real clock): the start
# menu, New Game, the difficulty, a base placed on the globe, the geoscape, the base
# screen, back to the geoscape. Coordinates: 640 x 360 (each screen pixel 2 x 2). The
# picture stands still (horizon/hz_plat.c "the screen"): the menus and the geoscape show
# rows 10-189, the base screens rows 20-199; the wheel moves it (2 steps up: rows 0-179).
0 wait xcom: ready for input
+1500 move 315 198
+500 shot
+300 click
+3000 move 320 90
+500 shot
+300 click
+5000 shot
+300 move 280 120
+500 click
+3000 shot
+300 {enter}
+4000 shot
# the INTERCEPT / BASES buttons sit in rows 0-21: the wheel shows them (rows 0-179)
+300 wheel 2
+500 move 577 38
+500 click
+5000 shot
# the base screen (rows 20-199 at once): GEOSCAPE, its bottom button
+300 move 580 350
+800 shot
+300 click
+5000 shot
# the geoscape answers the keyboard again: G, the graphs
+300 g
+4000 shot
